 "equipment_type": "Room air quality sensor",
 "applies_to": "Honeywell TR50 wall-mount indoor air quality sensors (temperature, humidity, CO2, PM2.5 / PM1.0 / PM10, TVOC) on BACnet MS/TP.",
 "summary": "The TR50 is a wall-mount indoor air quality sensor that reports temperature, humidity, CO2, particulates, TVOC and an air quality score on BACnet MS/TP (it also speaks Modbus and Sylk). Readings are Analog Inputs; alarm limits, deadbands, delays, offsets and display settings are writable Analog, Multistate and Binary Values, and each measurement has an out-of-range multistate. Which objects appear depends on the SKU (3-sensor models lack PM and TVOC).",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": "Same as the MS/TP MAC address",
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Objects created depend on the SKU: the 5-parameter models (TR50-5x) have PM2.5 and TVOC; the 3-parameter models do not.",
  "The guide prints CO2 names with the 2 as a subscript (e.g. 'CO 2'); names here join them (SS_AI_SensorReading_CO2). Name capitalisation (cfg / Cfg) is as printed.",
  "Defaults are given in the descriptions. Temperature-type settings follow the display unit (MV 101).",
  "CfgIsParaDisplayed (AV 381) is a bit mask of what the LCD shows; the bit meanings differ between TR50-5D and TR50-3D.",
  "The BTL PICS (Dec 2022) lists the same instances with ranges but no names."
 ],
